    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="0744" n="628" xml:id="pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13980.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-05T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 5, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Permanent Commission<anchor n="71" xml:id="d973-f1"/> today decided to call a
                    full meeting of the Convention for January 1st. At that meeting thirty
                    accredited Zapata delegates will participate.</p>
                <p>The Commission criticized President Gutiérrez for some of his appointments.
                    Leading members of the Commission for this reason predict the designation of
                    another provisional president during the first week of January.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d973-f1" n="71" xml:id="d973-f1-content">
                <p>See Mr. Canova’s November 14, 7 p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
